{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"An $\\blueE{\\text{exponent}}$ tells us how many factors of a $\\maroonD{\\text{base}}$ we should multiply to find the value of an expression.\n\nWe write exponential expressions like this: $\\maroonD{\\text{base}}^\\blueE{\\text{exponent}}$\n\nFor example,\n\n$\\maroonD{4}^\\blueE{3}=\\maroonD{4} \\times \\maroonD{4} \\times \\maroonD{4}$\n\nLet's use this definition to decide if each equation is true or false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n5^2 \u0026= 5 \\times 5\n\\\\\\\\\n2^5 \u0026= 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2\n\\end{align}$\n\nSo, $5^2=2^5$ is false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"By definition, $5^2 = 5 \\times 5$ is true.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$2^5 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2$ \n\nSo,  $2^5=5+5$ is false.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"[[☃ categorizer 3]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"categorizer 3":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"categories":["True","False"],"items":["$5^2=2^5$","$5^2=5\\times5$","$2^5=5+5$"],"linterContext":{"contentType":"","highlightLint":false,"paths":[],"stack":[]},"randomizeItems":false,"static":false,"values":[1,0,1]},"static":true,"type":"categorizer","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Determine whether each equation is true or false.**\n\n[[☃ categorizer 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"categorizer 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"categories":["True","False"],"items":["$5^2=2^5$","$5^2=5\\times5$","$2^5=5+5$"],"linterContext":{"contentType":"","highlightLint":false,"paths":[],"stack":[]},"randomizeItems":false,"static":false,"values":[1,0,1]},"static":false,"type":"categorizer","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
